“This is the main extraction section. It reads each unsubscribe record and captures details such as the GMPI ID, phone ID, program ID, unsubscribe date, source, and phone creation and update dates.”
Then explain the delta logic:
“We do not pull the entire history during every run. The script uses a delta start date, which represents the latest unsubscribe date already processed. Only records after that timestamp and up to the current execution time are included.
This prevents us from repeatedly processing the same members and makes the report more efficient.”
Show DELTA_START_DATETIME and DELTA_END_DATETIME
Say:
“Here, the start timestamp comes from the last successfully processed report, and the end timestamp is captured when the current run begins. So the report covers one clearly defined processing window.”
Then explain the template logic:
“For every newly unsubscribed member, the script also checks the outbound message history to identify the most recent applicable template.
It first checks the current outbound-message endpoint and then the archive endpoint if needed. It skips unsubscribe confirmation messages and the welcome message because those are not the actual campaign message that we want to associate with the opt-out.”
Show fetch_last_sent_template
